  "id": "Compound::DB06694 - Gene::150",
  "verbalization": "Xylometazoline is shown to bind to Adra2c, a variant of the Adrenergic Receptor, and this binding is associated with the participation in Alpha-2 adrenergic receptor activity, which in turn is linked to Adra2a. The evidence suggests a mechanistic pathway where Xylometazoline modulates the activity of Adra2c, which is a functional component of the Alpha-2 adrenergic receptor pathway. This pathway is ultimately linked to Adra2a, indicating a potential role for Xylometazoline in influencing the function of Adra2a through its interaction with Adra2c. The cumulative scores from the three paths support a consistent mechanism of action, where Xylometazoline exerts its effects via a shared intermediate, Adra2c, which is part of the broader Alpha-2 adrenergic receptor signaling cascade. The integration of these pathways highlights a plausible mechanism by which Xylometazoline may interact with Adra2a, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct involvement of Adra2a in this process.",
